This directory expects a file named exactly:

    stackchan_server_public_key.pem

containing the RSA public key (PEM format, e.g. "-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY----- ... -----END PUBLIC KEY-----")
of the self-hosted StackChan `server/` deployment this firmware talks to. It is the
`rsa.server.public` value from that server's config (e.g. `~/secrets/stackchan/config/config.yaml`
on the deployment host) -- NOT the private key.

This file is gitignored (see firmware/.gitignore) because it's specific to one self-hosted
deployment, the same way sdkconfig.defaults.local's CONFIG_STACKCHAN_SERVER_URL override is --
it has no meaningful "default" to ship upstream. The build will fail with a missing-file error
from EMBED_TXTFILES (see main/CMakeLists.txt) until you create the real file here.

This key is used by main/hal/utils/secret_logic/secret_logic.cpp's generate_auth_token() to
RSA-OAEP-SHA256-encrypt the device's auth token, matching server/internal/web_socket/web_socket.go's
GetMac() decryption on the server side.
